{"_id":"68a7362f8ec3d8323af1c516","nodeId":"GHKAY9gOykEbxkEeR30wL","roadmapSlug":"python","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:26.571Z","description":"# pyproject.toml\n\nThis file is used to define the project configuration and dependencies. It is a configuration file that contains metadata about the project, such as its name, version, dependencies, and build settings. The `pyproject.toml` file is used by tools like `poetry` and `flit` to manage Python projects and their dependencies.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Writing pyproject.toml files","url":"https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/writing-pyproject-toml/","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae365"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:09.455Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e33faacf8c05faf5e1fd0","title":"DataCamp - Python Programming Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/L0YnzL"},{"_id":"6a5e33fdacf8c05faf5e2124","title":"DataCamp - Python Developer","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/vDW623"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python/content/GHKAY9gOykEbxkEeR30wL.md"}